   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to location of certain wind electric generation facilities",
    "basePrintNo": "S1755",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1755-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §168, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1755\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the public service law, in relation\nto location of certain wind electric generation facilities\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis legislation would prohibit the construction or operation of a\nwind generating facility located within forty miles of an airfield or\nairbase.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends Section 168 of the public service law to prohibit the\nconstruction or operation of a wind generating facility located within\nforty miles of an airfield or airbase under jurisdiction of the\nDepartment of Defense which is in active use. This section also covers\nair traffic control radar sites, weather radar sites, or aircraft\nnavigations aids which are owned or operated by the DoD and are\npermanent land-based structures at a fixed location.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nWind generating facilities located in close proximity of airfields and\nairbases pose significant concerns both in the current operation of an\nairbase, but more importantly the possibility exists that these\nturbines could seriously imperil these airbases and the operations\nthey take part in now and in the future. When the Federal government\nundergoes Base Realignment and Closures (BRAC) it is important that\nthese military facilities are not imperiled by encroachments such as\nwind turbines.\n\nA recent report out of Corpus Christi has shed light onto the negative\nimpact wind turbines have on radar readings and installations in light\nof this it is critical to take into consideration the proximity these\nwind turbines have to an airfield or airbase.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
